You could prevent the transformation by wearing gloves, but as they would
also turn to gold you've have to take care which you put on.  Metal gloves
would retain the same hinges, rivets, etc., so they would be no problem, and
fabric gloves would turn to gold mesh and retain their flexibility.  The
humdinger would be leather gloves, which would turn into solid and relatively
inflexible gold sheeting.  You might even find yourself unable to get them
off.

Maybe in addition to the Midas touch the Dev Team (blessed be their names)
could add the ability to make gloves out of corpses with the intrinsic No
Polymorph, that wouldn't turn to gold.

Note that if we get the Midas touch _without_ a way of blocking it, we'd all
starve to death just like the original almost did.


